    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 66 tests pass, including the new `Cp54Tests` and the unchanged `Cp18Tests` (hard rejection at 50) and `Cp22Tests` (bulk warning). BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag on `POST /api/owners`, set true when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), following the existing OfficeFloor function-injection pattern used for the other warning flags.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`AssignCapacityWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 counts existing owners in the built owner's city (case-insensitive, the same match `RequireOwnerCityCapacity` uses) and sets `capacityWarning = true` when the count is in `[40, 50)`. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the count reflects only pre-existing owners.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired a `capacityWarning` step into the pipeline right after `build` (so the city is set) and before the save/response steps.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with accessor/mutator, mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (MapStruct maps it by name; the response then returns it and GET reads it back).\n\n5. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column so the persisted value survives the write/read round-trip the acceptance tests exercise.\n\nThe hard 409 rejection at 50 is untouched \u2014 it runs earlier in the pipeline, so a full city never reaches the warning step.",
